# Globs an agent may not edit without a human decision (repo-relative, glob).
# One per line. The preToolUse guard denies the edit and explains why.
#
# The CLI can enforce a second, coarser layer on the same idea without a hook:
#   copilot --deny-tool='write(.env)' --deny-tool='write(migrations)'
# The hook is here because it gives the agent a reason it can act on.
.env
.env.*
**/secrets.*
.github/copilot/protected-paths
.github/hooks/**
.github/workflows/**
infra/**
**/infra/**
migrations/**
**/migrations/**
